cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "energy-proxy: pre-registered single-case field study of an RTP/DTOD/5CP-aware HVAC controller"
abstract: >-
  Code, telemetry pipeline, and analysis pipeline for a pre-registered single-case
  experimental-design (SCED) field study comparing an RTP/DTOD/5CP-risk-aware HVAC
  controller against a household's existing programmable-thermostat schedule, run as a
  24-week A/B/A/B alternation (summer through fall 2026) in a single ComEd Hourly Pricing
  household. The binding pre-registration is the SCED rebaseline spec, frozen at the OSF
  filing commit.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chris
    family-names: dePaola
repository-code: "https://github.com/FireDevPro/energy-stack"
license: MIT
version: "osf-prereg-2026-05-31"
date-released: "2026-05-31"
keywords:
  - HVAC
  - demand response
  - real-time pricing
  - single-case experimental design
  - n-of-1
  - ComEd Hourly Pricing
  - PJM 5CP
